From: OddBlueDog <3959851+OddBlueDog@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 11:40:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mac80211: mark a txq for its wake under the queue stop lock

ieee80211_tx_dequeue() read the hardware queue's stop reasons under
queue_stop_reason_lock and, finding the queue stopped, marked the txq
dirty after dropping the lock. __ieee80211_wake_queue() clears the stop
under that lock and then wakes the driver for the txqs it finds marked. A
wake that ran between the unlock and the mark found nothing to wake.

Mark under the lock, and only take it when the queue is stopped.

From OddBlueDog/openwrt milkflint-25.12 401.
Downstream patch, no upstream equivalent: absent from mainline
(v6.18, v7.0, v7.2-rc4, v7.3, v7.4-rc4) and from wireless-next HEAD on
2026-11-28. Taken from OddBlueDog/openwrt milkflint-25.12, commit c2bc69efb501;
no stable or mainline tracking, so drop it by hand if a real fix lands.

---
--- a/net/mac80211/tx.c
+++ b/net/mac80211/tx.c
@@ -3900,14 +3900,24 @@
 		return NULL;
 
 begin:
-	spin_lock_irqsave(&local->queue_stop_reason_lock, flags);
-	q_stopped = local->queue_stop_reasons[q];
-	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&local->queue_stop_reason_lock, flags);
+	/*
+	 * A stopped queue is rare (a scan's visit to another channel, a
+	 * reset), so only that case takes the lock. The txq is marked for
+	 * the wake under the lock __ieee80211_wake_queue() clears the stop
+	 * under: either that wake finds the mark when it goes looking for
+	 * txqs, or the queue is seen awake here. Marked after the unlock, a
+	 * wake in between found nothing, and the txq's frames waited for
+	 * whatever next brought the driver round.
+	 */
+	if (unlikely(READ_ONCE(local->queue_stop_reasons[q]))) {
+		spin_lock_irqsave(&local->queue_stop_reason_lock, flags);
+		q_stopped = local->queue_stop_reasons[q];
+		if (q_stopped)
+			set_bit(IEEE80211_TXQ_DIRTY, &txqi->flags);
+		spin_unlock_irqrestore(&local->queue_stop_reason_lock, flags);
 
-	if (unlikely(q_stopped)) {
-		/* mark for waking later */
-		set_bit(IEEE80211_TXQ_DIRTY, &txqi->flags);
-		return NULL;
+		if (q_stopped)
+			return NULL;
 	}
 
 	spin_lock_bh(&fq->lock);
